.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-LIST-MY-ACCOUNTS 1 "November 2026" "euclid-cli 2.1.3" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-list-my-accounts \- list the accounts you may work in
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eam list-my-accounts
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the accounts the signed-in user may work in: their home account
(the one they were registered in), and every account named by a role
granted to them or to a group they belong to.
.PP
Unlike
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-accounts (1),
which is an administrator's view of every account there is, this one is
about the caller and needs no privileges. An administrator gets every
account, since being an administrator is permission everywhere rather
than a grant anywhere.
.PP
The answer also carries
.IR homeAccountId :
the account to work in when nothing else has been chosen.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The accounts are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
The server could not be reached, or there is no valid session.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eam list-my-accounts
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-accounts (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-grants (1)
